Backdoor Accounts & Config Changes
• sec_monitor superuser in ns.conf
• /bin/sh with mode 6555 (SUID)
• Unauthorized AddHandler / SetHandler / Alias in httpd.conf
• php_flag or php_value in httpd.conf
• Cron entries in /var/cron/tabs/ pointing to unknown scripts
• Modified /nsconfig/rc.netscaler or /nsconfig/nsafter.sh

Malware
WHIPSHOT — PHP webshell. Hides as .ico/.sig/.deb files. Uses HTTP_X_UX headers. Returns fake 404s.
SLAPSHOT — Python tunneler. Creates /tmp/.uxdport and /tmp/.uxdlock. Runs on localhost, auto-exits after 10 min idle.
update_c08937.pl — Perl script. Creates sec_monitor account, steals config, deploys webshell, sets /bin/sh to SUID. Self-deletes.
main.py / customsnmpd — Python reverse shell to 45.141.21.130:443. Overwrites legit /var/python/bin/customsnmpd.
Sliver — Off-the-shelf C2. FreeBSD binary at /var/tmp/.host. Phones home to pylrk.cc.
Platypus — Off-the-shelf C2. Enrolls at entretiensol.com. Uses mDNS on UDP/5353.

Hunt Checklist
[ ] Look for sec_monitor account in ns.conf
[ ] Check /bin/sh permissions — should NOT be 6555
[ ] Check for /tmp/.uxdport and /tmp/.uxdlock (SLAPSHOT)
[ ] Check /var/netscaler/logon/ for any .ico, .sig, .deb, or .php files that shouldn't be there
[ ] Check httpd.conf for unauthorized PHP handlers (AddHandler, SetHandler, Alias)
[ ] Look for weird Python processes that aren't stock NetScaler
[ ] Check /var/python/bin/customsnmpd — compare size/hash to known good
[ ] Check for /tmp/update_result_3567cs.tgz (stolen config archive)
[ ] Check /var/core/.ns-cache/ for stolen certs
[ ] Check cron tabs and startup scripts (rc.netscaler, nsafter.sh) for persistence
[ ] Grep logs for pitboss PPE unexpectedly died (log poisoning)
[ ] Grep logs for username=anonymous or ${IFS} (injection payloads)
[ ] Grep logs for nsaaad crashes with exit 0x8a (SAML bug / 88779)
[ ] Check if SAML is configured, if yes, confirm you're on 73.41/64.28
[ ] Run Poppelgaard's checker script - https://github.com/ThomasPoppelgaard/netscaler-ctx697096-checker
